expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{prop:cd-kl}
The micro-closure deficit can be written as
\begin{equation}
\mathsf{CD}_\tau(\Pi)
=
\sum_{x \in \mathcal{X}}
\pi(x)\,
D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\bigl(
p_x^{(\tau)}
\,\|\,
\bar p_{\Pi(x)}^{(\tau)}
\bigr),
\label{eq:cd-kl}
\end{equation}
where, in the finite case,
\[
D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p\|q) := \sum_{y' \in \mathcal{Y}} p(y') \log \frac{p(y')}{q(y')},
\]
with the convention $0 \log (0/q)=0$.

