expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{def:tau-closed}
A packaging $\Pi$ is \emph{$\tau$-closed} if for every $x,x' \in \mathcal{X}$ with $\Pi(x)=\Pi(x')$, one has
\begin{equation}
p_x^{(\tau)} = p_{x'}^{(\tau)}
\quad\text{as distributions on }\mathcal{Y}.
\label{eq:tau-closed}
\end{equation}

